{"Blacklisted guest email addresses are normalized to lowercase, but incoming guest emails are compared as-is, so case differences will bypass the blacklist check": 0.9425807595252991, "The team-privilege check uses a logical AND between 'is team admin' and 'is team owner', which means a user must be both to be authorized instead of either, incorrectly blocking legitimate admins or owners from adding guests": 0.939704954624176, "The email notification function is called with the original guest list instead of the filtered list of actually added guests, causing emails to be sent to already-attending or blacklisted addresses that were not added to the booking": 0.9880183935165405, "The invalid-email error flag is only ever set to true and never reset on a successful validation, so once an invalid input has occurred the error message will continue to be shown even after the user corrects the emails and a valid submission is made": 0.915930986404419, "When sending emails after adding guests, new attendees receive AttendeeScheduledEmail built from calendarEvent without stripping additionalNotes when hideCalendarNotes is true, unlike the other scheduling flows, meaning newly added guests can see calendar notes that should be hidden": 0.7353572249412537, "The subject prop is set to the i18n key 'guests_added_event_type_subject' and passed straight through to BaseEmailHtml, so recipients will see the raw key as the email subject instead of a localized, formatted string": 0.36924266815185547, "By hardcoding title, headerType, and subject while spreading props afterwards, any title, headerType, or subject passed in via props will override these values, which is likely unintended for a dedicated 'add guests' email template": 0.8339141607284546}